  "_annotate_note": "annotate_query marks a QUERY proteome for the proteome-annotate workflow. annotate_ladder is the organism's full Swiss-Prot OC lineage, narrow-to-broad; any rung is a valid --exclude_clade, and references are cached by CLADE NAME so minus-Chordata is one file shared by human, mouse, chicken, zebrafish and ciona. annotate_clade is the default rung. swissprot counts are measured from uniprot_sprot.dat.gz dated 2025-07-03: reviewed, pe1 (protein-level existence), exp_ft (entries with >=1 ECO:0000269 feature), and feature totals split experimental vs by-similarity. Evidence level is a STRATUM, not a filter -- all levels are scored and reported separately, because filtering to experimental ranks species by curation depth (ciona keeps 1 entry) rather than by biology.",
